# Ensembl Go
#
# These rules broadly mirror the exclusions in scripts/archive_github_snapshot.sh,
# which builds a recovery snapshot: unpack it and get back to development without this
# repository. Keep the two in step — if something is added here, consider whether the
# snapshot should skip it too — with one deliberate asymmetry, noted at the docs
# entries below. The snapshot fails if any tracked file is missing from it, so an
# over-broad exclusion there cannot go unnoticed; the reverse is not checked.

# --- OS and editor noise ---
.DS_Store
*~
*.bak
*_bak
*.swp

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.tox/

# --- Node ---
node_modules/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.vite/
.vite-temp/
coverage/

# --- Build output (all regenerable) ---
frontend/dist/
electron/dist/
electron/dist_backend/
electron/build_backend/
electron/build_log*.txt
# Staged MAFFT bundle, rebuilt by `npm run prepare:mafft`. Everything else under
# electron/build/ (icons, entitlements) is source and must stay tracked.
electron/build/mafft_bin/

# --- Runtime state ---
backend/cache/
backend/output_dir/
backend/local_data/
backend/debug_backend.txt

# --- Genome data does not belong in backend/data ---
# The application ships no sample genomes for real use: users download assemblies
# through the download view or supply their own. backend/data holds only the
# classification artifacts that decide species grouping, which ARE tracked (a couple of
# megabytes, read at run time by backend/project_classifier.py and
# backend/taxonomy_classifier.py). These patterns are a guard, so a stray FASTA or GFF3
# left in that directory during development cannot be committed or bundled by
# build-backend.js. They are anchored, so they only match the top level.
#
# The deliberate exceptions are the two tutorial genomes, which ARE tracked:
#
#   backend/data/demo_genome/  — twenty-two kilobases of made-up assembly that the
#                                Getting Started tutorial installs in place of a real
#                                download. Built by scripts/build_demo_genome.py.
#   backend/data/grch38_reg4/  — six hundred kilobytes: half a megabase of real
#                                chromosome 1 around REG4, at its true coordinates, for
#                                the genome browser tutorial. Built by
#                                scripts/build_grch38_slice.py.
#
# Regenerate and commit rather than editing by hand. See docs/TUTORIALS.md.
backend/data/*.fa
backend/data/*.fai
backend/data/*.gff3
backend/data/*.gz
backend/data/*.bgz
backend/data/*.gzi

# --- Experimental Rust/WASM renderer ---
# The Cargo project stays tracked; only the build directory is ignored, at roughly
# 790 MB. pkg/ is wasm-pack's output and is NOT tracked, because wasm-pack writes its
# own `*` .gitignore inside it. The snapshot does carry pkg/, so recovering does not
# depend on having a Rust toolchain to hand.
frontend/rust/*/target/

# --- Vendored 3D structure viewer ---
# pdbe-molstar's prebuilt bundle, ~6 MB, copied out of node_modules by
# frontend/scripts/copy-structure-viewer.js. The script is tracked; its output
# is not.
backend/static/structure/vendor/

# --- Snapshots, vendored clones, scratch ---
exports/
temp_repos/
ensembl_local_github_*/
test-data/

# --- Local tooling config ---
# Personal settings stay out; shared tooling under .claude/ is tracked. The pattern has
# to exclude the *contents* rather than the directory, or git never descends far enough
# to see the exception below.
# A shared .claude/settings.json, if added, should be tracked.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
#
# These three are the deliberate asymmetry with the snapshot: untracked here, but
# included there. They are working documents that exist in no other copy, so a
# recovery archive without them loses them for good. The genome-links table was
# tracked until it was moved here; no script regenerates it, so the snapshot names
# it explicitly rather than sweeping all of outputs/, which is scratch.
docs/browsing-controls-handoff.md
docs/tutorial-builder-genome-playlists-handoff.md
outputs/alignment-explorer-genome-links/44_mammals_epo_release115_genome_links.tsv

